# Wave W17-W (Route 211): lotus post — a meditation-circle marker post at the circle’s approach: a weathered post carrying one pale carved ring band and a flat stone cap, the circle’s mark kept plain so the stones of the circle itself stay the design’s, not the post’s (design: standing stones around a great stone lotus on its own bluff — the shipped bluff carries no stone circle, so the posts mark the approach and invent nothing beyond it). On lotus turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s banded posts by the ring and the cap: bands warn and measure, this post only stands quiet at a quiet place.
